I like this idea. Further suggestions:
Monster parts that are already seperate (worm tooth, unicorn horn,
dragon scales) should not appear simply as a result of killing the monster.
They should be the result of hacking it up.
I agree that any edged weapon should be usable for hacking up monsters,
but scalpels should do it in less time and have less of a chance of
damaging the special organs.  Perhaps daggers should be in-between in
effectiveness, kind of like opening tins with them...
Only complete monster corpses should be sacrificable.  That way, we get
nice dilemmas like "Hmm, I could sacrifice this non-coaligned unicorn for
big brownie points with my god, but I really need that horn..."
Of course, if the monster is large, and your weapon is ill-suited, there's
a good chance that it will start to rot before you're through...

